cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the manuscript below and the archived release of this repository (concept doi:10.5281/zenodo.24106082, resolves to the latest version)."
title: "directional-tail-excess: a distribution-level test separating subpopulation selection from a population-wide state transition"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a distribution-level test of paired single-cell transcriptomes.
  For every patient, programme and interval, quantiles of a programme score are measured
  before and after treatment and normalised by the baseline interquartile range. The
  signed trailing-end excess separates a subpopulation selection event, which moves one
  end of the distribution, from a population-wide state transition, which moves every
  quantile by the same amount. The pipeline produces all figures and numbers of the
  accompanying manuscript across three independent neoadjuvant breast cancer cohorts.
